# Reference: a snapshot point, something worth saving, one snapshot taken now, and a look at the dashboard.
# (Run on the crash node, target redis://redis-nopersist:6379. After Verify: kill and up the node to watch score:final come back.)
CONFIG GET save
CONFIG GET dir
# snapshot when 1000 keys changed within 60 seconds; this is live only, a restart forgets it
CONFIG SET save "60 1000"
SET score:final 24
INFO persistence
# a snapshot now, in a child process, so the server keeps answering
BGSAVE
# the snapshot is written by a child process: BLPOP on a key that does not exist just waits half a second so that it has finished (you can simply look again a second later)
BLPOP wait:half:a:second 0.5
LASTSAVE
CONFIG GET save
INFO persistence
LASTSAVE
